   "evidence": "`code/TauCeti/Combinatorics/Young/Diagram.lean:293-300`: `theorem finite_Iic (\u03bc : YoungDiagram) : (Set.Iic \u03bc).Finite` \u2014 docstring \"A Young diagram has finitely many sub-diagrams\". `code/TauCeti/Combinatorics/Young/Interlacing.lean:123-131`: `interlacingShapes n \u03bc := Set.Finite.toFinset (s := {\u03bd | InterlacedBy \u03bc \u03bd \u2227 \u03bd.colLen 0 \u2264 n}) ((finite_Iic \u03bc).subset fun _ h => Set.mem_Iic.mpr h.1.le)` with `mem_interlacingShapes := Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _`. `finite_Iic` is in the import closure: PowerSumExpansion \u2192 MurnaghanNakayama \u2192 `public import TauCeti.Combinatorics.Young.RimHook` \u2192 `public import TauCeti.Combinatorics.Young.Corner` \u2192 `public import TauCeti.Combinatorics.Young.Diagram`. `IsRimHook.le : \u03bd \u2264 \u03bc` is a field (`RimHook.lean:113`).",
   "file": "TauCeti/RingTheory/MvPolynomial/Symmetric/Schur/PowerSumExpansion.lean",
   "fix": "Define `noncomputable def rimHookSubdiagrams (\u03bc : YoungDiagram) (r : \u2115) : Finset YoungDiagram := Set.Finite.toFinset (s := {\u03bd | \u03bd.card + r = \u03bc.card \u2227 \u03bc.IsRimHook \u03bd}) ((YoungDiagram.finite_Iic \u03bc).subset fun _ h => Set.mem_Iic.mpr h.2.le)` (using the `IsRimHook.le` field), and replace the proof of `mem_rimHookSubdiagrams` by `Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _`. Both `open scoped Classical in` lines (87, 92) then become unnecessary; the `hset` step in the main proof is unaffected since it only uses `mem_rimHookSubdiagrams`.",
   "issue": "`rimHookSubdiagrams` re-derives the finiteness of a set of sub-diagrams by enumerating `Finset.image (diagramOf (n := \u03bc.card - r)) Finset.univ` and filtering, and `mem_rimHookSubdiagrams` (line 95) then has to supply a `toPartition` witness to undo that enumeration. TauCeti already has the combinator for this: `YoungDiagram.finite_Iic` (every sub-diagram set is finite) composed with `Set.Finite.toFinset`, which is precisely how `YoungDiagram.interlacingShapes` is defined.",
